# INSTALLATION

On Linux (GCC 15+ defaults to C23, so pass `-std=gnu17`; `-Ud_thread_local`
is required on Linux so `libperl` and extensions avoid static TLS):

    ./Configure -des -Dusethreads -Ud_thread_local \
        -Dprefix=$HOME/localperl -Accflags='-std=gnu17' -Doptimize='-O2 -g'
    make -j$(nproc)
    TEST_JOBS=$(nproc) make test_harness
    make install

On macOS:

    ./Configure -des -Dusethreads -Dprefix=$HOME/localperl -Doptimize='-O2 -g'
    make -j$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu)
    TEST_JOBS=$(sysctl -n hw.ncpu) make test_harness
    make install

For a Profile-Guided Optimization build (add `-Dusenative` if the binary
only needs to run on the build machine):

    ./Configure -des -Dusethreads -Ud_thread_local \
        -Dprefix=$HOME/localperl -Accflags='-std=gnu17' -Dusepgo
    make -j$(nproc) pgo

On macOS, drop `-Ud_thread_local` and `-Accflags='-std=gnu17'` from the
PGO configure line.

To run the standalone kernel-runtime, acceleration, and multi-threading
test suites:

    make -C krt test
    make -C accel test
    ./perl -I. -Ilib -MTest::Harness -e 'runtests(@ARGV)' t/mt/*.t

If you run into any trouble whatsoever or need a customized build, read the
detailed instructions in the `INSTALL` file and the platform `README.*`
files that came with this distribution.

Once you have Perl installed, a wealth of documentation is available through
the `perldoc` tool:

    perldoc perl


# IF YOU RUN INTO TROUBLE

Perl is a large and complex system that's used for everything from
knitting to rocket science.  If you run into trouble with `perl5-mt`
features, please check `MT_README.md` and `MT_DESIGN.md` first and open an
issue with your platform, compiler, and test output.  For upstream Perl 5
issues and releases, see https://github.com/Perl/perl5/issues and
https://www.cpan.org/src/.

If you want to submit a patch to the perl source, see `CONTRIBUTING.md` and
the "SUPER QUICK PATCH GUIDE" in `pod/perlhack.pod`.

